{"title":"2009 Zhautykov International Olympiad Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a convex hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> with an area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, prove that:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d34e299c8bf6393bbc5553f97c9a44c6ee23bcb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC\\cdot(BD + BF - DF) + CE\\cdot(BD + DF - BF) + AE\\cdot(BF + DF - BD)\\geq 2\\sqrt {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"669\" height=\"21\" />.</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Lemma\">Lemma</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Lemma\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, let's set aside the original problem and introduce the \"Gergonne point\" and its distance to the vertices.\n</p><p>Let the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> touch <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. By Ceva's theorem, it is easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> are concurrent at a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, which we call the Gergonne point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1509090255f169edf94b63df3e.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/91/1509090255f169edf94b63df3e.gif\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"329\" height=\"261\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/4/c34fa792cf5bd24cfe744311f83d479c0925b98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=AF=x$\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f8d4754b3fc848f180359219c77d91493bb77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF=BD=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58f18b0e0461258974bd05bfb2944e1313fd6bbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=CE=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />. As shown in the figure, by Stewart's theorem, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1627c0c669128ef14ac26b46c881aee349fe24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD^2=\\frac{(z+x)^2y+(x+y)^2z}{y+z}-yz=\\frac{x(4yz+zx+xy)}{y+z},\\]\" width=\"442\" height=\"43\" />\nIn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, by Menelaus' theorem, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7e20ed4d703068c2dcff6543df3838b2c873615.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AQ}{AD-AQ}\\cdot \\frac y{y+z}\\cdot \\frac zx=1,\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"41\" />\nSolving this, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5507b384e37480bb73acac0a98bdf32b2af05a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AQ=\\frac{x(y+z)}{yz+zx+xy}\\cdot AD=\\frac{x\\sqrt{x(y+z)(4yz+zx+xy)}}{yz+zx+xy}.\\]\" width=\"452\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Noting that by AM-GM inequality, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sqrt{x(y+z)(4yz+zx+xy)}&amp;=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\sqrt{3x(y+z)(4yz+zx+xy)} \\\\\n&amp; \\leqslant \\frac{3x(y+z)+4yz+zx+xy}{2\\sqrt3} \\\\\n&amp; =\\frac{2(yz+zx+xy)}{\\sqrt3},\n\\end{align*}\nwe get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f328a28317d7146fc9e3aca548d9cd0610877d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AQ\\leqslant \\frac2{\\sqrt3}x,\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"41\" />\nThus, we obtain the following lemma.\n</p><p>Lemma: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the Gergonne point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2f25ebbb22b3c56b8368645fc42a8840e1d8ad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB+AC-BC\\geqslant \\sqrt3AQ.\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Returning_to_the_original_problem\">Returning to the original problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Returning to the original problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1509090255851ede02a626c22a.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/bd/1509090255851ede02a626c22a.gif\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"296\" height=\"235\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be the Gergonne point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc4a1ecf2193896680e5e73b698d50e779548b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. As shown in the figure, by the lemma, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f2cf9fe5a893aad39324561560b39c4fb506a3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC\\cdot(BD + BF - DF)\\geqslant AC\\cdot\\sqrt3BK\\geqslant 2\\sqrt3S_{ABCK},\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"21\" />\nSimilarly, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/52901f76992bc9967662a3b4ac8748365e9e57db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE\\cdot(BD + DF - BF)\\geqslant 2\\sqrt3S_{CDEK}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"304\" height=\"24\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed2055a347c213bab2e0ccb75b2d0c14f538478b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE\\cdot(BF + DF - BD)\\geqslant 2\\sqrt3S_{EFAK}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"302\" height=\"24\" />, adding these together, we get the desired result.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017222140\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 154/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5599/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:29623:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017222140 and revision id 232867. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}